   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 5083652,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 1113235,
    "poster_id": 213285,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > be an acute triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1187dd9239dad50242ec0cea3577b78253c225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AB| \\neq |AC|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" > and the midpoints of segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada6f54288b7a2cdd299eba0055f8c8d19916b4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AB]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/0936990e6625d65357ca51006c08c9fe3e04ba0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" > be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > resp. <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" >.</span> The circumcircles of the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\"  width=\"44\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/91275aa1f85be8f39ea3ae3cef68f10100fc664b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCE$\"  width=\"43\" height=\"12\" > intersect the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\"  width=\"43\" height=\"13\" > in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > resp. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" > with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd0a382775e56bd050d7eb432e0bdaebfbafa6fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P \\neq D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed69421328573329f794fd2a77c5af00c020279b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q \\neq E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" >.</span><br>\nProve <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408383d63ea93dafa6e92b8c78b6bfeb67ec5f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AP|=|AQ|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\n<i>(Notation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8d59296392ea2d3ac5c03686b0d5ef858d86b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\cdot|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" > denotes the length of a segment and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/9/579a0ec9e030cc17f3b2c9cd1510c9493b1813b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\cdot]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" > denotes the line segment.)</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $ABC$ be an acute triangle with $|AB| \\neq |AC|$ and the midpoints of segments $[AB]$ and $[AC]$ be $D$ resp. $E$. The circumcircles of the triangles $BCD$ and $BCE$ intersect the circumcircle of triangle $ADE$ in $P$ resp. $Q$ with $P \\neq D$ and $Q \\neq E$.\nProve $|AP|=|AQ|$.\n\n[i](Notation: $|\\cdot|$ denotes the length of a segment and $[\\cdot]$ denotes the line segment.)[/i]",
    "username": "Kezer",
    "post_number": 1,
    "post_format": "bbcode",
    "category_name": "High School Olympiads",
    "category_id": 6,
    "poster_avatar": "//avatar.artofproblemsolving.com/avatar_213285.jpg?t=1498485447"
