    "post_rendered": "Determine all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" > of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/7/ec778edf97100f3b19350d8a817317ebf1f391bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt[3]{7x^2-13xy+7y^2}=|x-y|+1.\\]\"  width=\"263\" height=\"22\" ><br>\n<i>Proposed by Titu Andreescu, USA</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Determine all pairs $(x, y)$ of positive integers such that \\[\\sqrt[3]{7x^2-13xy+7y^2}=|x-y|+1.\\]\n[i]Proposed by Titu Andreescu, USA[/i]",
