   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 5083659,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 1113240,
    "poster_id": 213285,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > be an acute triangle with the circumcircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" > and incenter <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" >.</span> The perpendicular through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" > in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d37413bae1973358eebff164711f292d16be56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI$\"  width=\"24\" height=\"12\" > intersects segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1d44f3905940ec53e7eebd2aa5e491eb9e3732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" > in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" > in <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" >.</span> In particular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > are on different sides of <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" >.</span> The parallel line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\"  width=\"23\" height=\"13\" > intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/7/7478949eb3c36f58ef0d04b3fb861a0451a56c4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AV$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" > in <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" >.</span><br>\nProve: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e1264947b8a96424d8ec23df523cc3ac3970b380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XI$\"  width=\"26\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\"  width=\"23\" height=\"13\" > are perpendicular to each other, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e1264947b8a96424d8ec23df523cc3ac3970b380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XI$\"  width=\"26\" height=\"12\" > intersects segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/0936990e6625d65357ca51006c08c9fe3e04ba0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" > in its midpoint <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\n<i>(Notation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/9/579a0ec9e030cc17f3b2c9cd1510c9493b1813b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\cdot]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" > denotes the line segment.)</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $ABC$ be an acute triangle with the circumcircle $k$ and incenter $I$. The perpendicular through $I$ in $CI$ intersects segment $[BC]$ in $U$ and $k$ in $V$. In particular $V$ and $A$ are on different sides of $BC$. The parallel line through $U$ to $AI$ intersects $AV$ in $X$.\nProve: If $XI$ and $AI$ are perpendicular to each other, then $XI$ intersects segment $[AC]$ in its midpoint $M$.\n\n[i](Notation: $[\\cdot]$ denotes the line segment.)[/i]",
    "username": "Kezer",
    "post_number": 1,
    "post_format": "bbcode",
    "category_name": "High School Olympiads",
    "category_id": 6,
    "poster_avatar": "//avatar.artofproblemsolving.com/avatar_213285.jpg?t=1498485447"
   }
